{"availability":"available","full":"sahilmenon/CFR-Poker-Bot","name":"CFR-Poker-Bot","description":"CFR and CFR+ solvers for Kuhn poker and Leduc Hold'em, validated against Kuhn's closed-form value of -1/18 by a best-response exploitability evaluator. Live browser demo.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-29T10:05:44Z","updated":"2026-09-18T14:36:34Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://poker.sahilmenon.com","topics":["cfr","counterfactual-regret-minimization","game-theory","imperfect-information-games","kuhn-poker","leduc-holdem","nash-equilibrium","poker","python"],"demo":"https://poker.sahilmenon.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:50:54.813Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T15:50:54.813Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T15:50:54.813Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T07:21:38.908Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T09:23:48.090Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T19:01:09.793Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T15:50:54.813Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Play it: poker.sahilmenon.com. The solved bot runs in your browser.","Counterfactual Regret Minimization (CFR and CFR+) solvers for two benchmark imperfect-information poker games, Kuhn poker and Leduc Hold'em. I built them from the original papers and checked them against ground truth: the solver reproduces Kuhn poker's closed-form game value of −1/18 and its analytic equilibrium family, and a best-response evaluator measures exploitability down to 9×10⁻⁴ chips/game on Kuhn and 1.5×10⁻³ on Leduc.","Most hobby CFR repos print a strategy and stop. This one checks its own answer: Kuhn poker is solved in closed form, so a correct solver has to reproduce −1/18, and mine does."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sahilmenon/CFR-Poker-Bot/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"90ed44bbb80249e9249202c6368f468f7e85828172b76e64b6aab5e728f356ff